Review written to `docs/reviews/weather/weather-01-resstock-ghi-no-upper-bound.md`.

**Key finding**: The ResStock CSV parser at `resstock_csv.rs:219` checks only `ghi_w_m2 < 0.0`, missing the `<= 1500` upper bound that EPW, TMY3, and PSM3 parsers all enforce. EnergyPlus itself validates no upper bound on GHI (only `< 0`), making HARES's 1500 W/m² limit a defensive improvement. The fix is a one-line change to add `!(0.0..=1500.0).contains(&ghi_w_m2)`.
